      "pronunciationText": "Last video ended on this curve: e to the x, over x plus one. At x equals minus one, the bottom is zero, and you can't divide by zero, so there's no curve there. A fraction like this works like average speed, distance over time, and you can't average over zero time. Now the slope at x equals zero. A quick guess: divide the derivatives. The top's derivative is e to the x, and the bottom's is one, so the guess gives a slope of one at x equals zero. But the tangent there is flat. So how do we really differentiate a quotient, and keep track of where it's defined?"
    },
